WEBVTT

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:03.040
This video covers reviewing
a draft note: checking it

00:00:03.040 --> 00:00:07.030
against the recording, correcting
it, and finishing your review.

00:00:07.280 --> 00:00:09.200
The transcript sits beside the note.

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:12.950
Search it for a word, then click a passage
to play the audio from that moment.

00:00:13.593 --> 00:00:16.393
Highlighted citations link
the note to the recording.

00:00:16.393 --> 00:00:19.263
Here, the note says
Mochi's weight was stable.

00:00:19.353 --> 00:00:23.113
Click the citation, and the
transcript and audio jump to that

00:00:23.113 --> 00:00:26.623
moment: her weight is actually
up a little since Tuesday.

00:00:26.873 --> 00:00:29.423
Choose Edit, correct
the wording, then Save.

00:00:30.027 --> 00:00:31.947
The editor uses Markdown.

00:00:31.947 --> 00:00:36.497
Select text and use the toolbar for
bold, italics, headings, or lists.

00:00:36.667 --> 00:00:39.947
Saving keeps your changes,
but the encounter stays open.

00:00:39.947 --> 00:00:42.497
When your review is
finished, choose Complete.

00:00:43.093 --> 00:00:45.413
For focused reading and
editing, choose Full

00:00:45.413 --> 00:00:48.533
screen, or press Command, Shift, F.

00:00:48.533 --> 00:00:50.043
Press Escape to return.

00:00:50.133 --> 00:00:52.043
The draft is a starting point.

00:00:52.213 --> 00:00:54.043
Your review is what makes it the record.
